From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: size the reconstruction buffer for 10-bit side data

cedrus_update_recon_format() builds the reconstruction format with
cedrus_prepare_format() alone, while the capture queue goes through
cedrus_calculate_format(), which additionally adds the codec's
extra_cap_size().  For H.265 that is the 2-bit plane of a 10-bit picture,
appended after the 8-bit planes.

So a 10-bit reconstruction buffer is allocated for its 8-bit planes only, and
the engine writes the 2-bit plane past the end of it.

No bug is reachable today: the reconstruction only gets its own buffer when the
scaler is running, cedrus_s_selection() refuses a compose rectangle for
anything but H.264, and H.264 has no extra_cap_size.  The two halves meet as
soon as the H.265 scaler is enabled, so fix the sizing first.

@@ -366,6 +366,16 @@
 	ctx->recon_fmt.bytesperline = 0;
 	ctx->recon_fmt.sizeimage = 0;
 	cedrus_prepare_format(&ctx->recon_fmt);
+
+	/*
+	 * Codecs with side data per capture buffer need it here too: the
+	 * reconstruction is a frame like any other.  H.265 appends the 2-bit
+	 * plane of a 10-bit picture after the 8-bit planes, and without this
+	 * the buffer is allocated for the 8-bit planes alone.
+	 */
+	if (ctx->current_codec && ctx->current_codec->extra_cap_size)
+		ctx->recon_fmt.sizeimage +=
+			ctx->current_codec->extra_cap_size(ctx, &ctx->recon_fmt);
 }
 
 /*

